## Summary

Executed order `O-260817-09` (legal wrapping of the client booking path), the only open order in `state/15_ORDERS.md` with status "принято"/"в работе" and a `feature/` branch that hadn't already been started by a prior run.

**Found the actual bug:** consent for browser/MAX clients (non-Telegram) was completely broken — `checkConsentRequired('', ...)` silently returned an empty consent text, and `saveConsent('')` wrote nothing to the client record (only a garbage `TelegramClient` row keyed on an empty string, overwritten by every anonymous visitor). Fixed by keying consent to a channel-agnostic identity (`{clientId, telegramUserId}`) resolved directly against `DiaryClient`.

**Delivered**, PR [`compas-psy/cmpas.ru#100`](https://github.com/compas-psy/cmpas.ru/pull/100), branch `feature/client-legal`, not merged:
- Consent tied to the client record, not the channel, plus a server-side gate in `bookSession` (didn't exist before).
- Consent checkbox no longer links to the Privacy Policy (that's now a separate informational link).
- New consent text names the psychologist as data operator and КОМПАС as processor-by-instruction (data migration, versioned); profile page warns if the psychologist's name is blank.
- Working "revoke consent" button on the client's own page — notifies the psychologist, blocks new self-booking until re-consent, preserves history.
- Point 5 (service vs. marketing messages) confirmed not applicable — no marketing message exists in the codebase to gate.

18 new tests, 58/58 total passing; 0 new TypeScript/ESLint errors vs. `main`; `next build` clean; migration verified idempotent against a real Postgres. Updated and pushed `state/15_ORDERS.md` and the runner log to `compas-ops` main. Did not merge or deploy anything.
